From 7d8e182cb6e4fdd7fba19977161e7d1ecac864ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:51:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] ipa: simple: Add noise reduction and sharpening

Drive the GPU debayer's noise reduction and sharpening pass from a new
Detail algorithm: the bilateral range sigma grows with the square root
of the total gain (analogue times digital), up to 0.15 of full scale,
and the unsharp mask amount falls as 1 / (1 + log2(gain) / 3), so a
dim scene is smoothed rather than sharpened. The tuning file gives the
base strengths; without a Detail entry the picture is untouched.
Support the Sharpness control as a factor on the amount, from 0 to 4.

Enable it on the Pixel 7 Pro's cameras with an amount of 0.6 and a
sigma of 0.015 at unity gain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
